+### [3D Cube Projection and Rasterization](6678-3d-cube-projection-and-rasterization.md)
+3D Cube Projection and Rasterization is a software rendering technique that transforms the geometric faces of a 3D voxel cube into 2D screen space and draws them as filled polygons. It solves the problem of visualizing individual volumetric cells by treating them as explicit opaque or semi-opaque quads rather than sampling them via raycasting or texture mapping. It differs from hardware-accelerated rasterization by performing all matrix multiplications, perspective division, and pixel writing in software, and from standard raycasting by relying on explicit polygonal face projection and depth culling rather than per-pixel ray traversal.
 
