 ### Screen Space Area Calculation
-#### definition
-Calculates the projected area of a tetrahedron in normalized screen space to determine refinement criteria or culling. Uses cross products to compute wedge areas, which are twice the triangle area, then divides by four [S5, unofficial].
-#### step
-Project tetrahedron vertices $T, L, R, B$ to screen space using camera projection: $T \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(T)$, $L \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(L)$, $R \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(R)$, $B \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(B)$. Calculate area sum using cross products of vertex vectors: $\text{area} \leftarrow |(L-T)\times(R-T)|+|(R-T)\times(B-T)|$. Add remaining terms: $\text{area} \leftarrow \text{area}+|(B-T)\times(L-T)|+|(L-B)\times(R-B)|$. Return final area divided by 4: $\text{return area} / 4$ [S5, unofficial].
-#### pitfall
-Triangles cover the total area twice in projection, and cross products yield wedge areas (twice triangle area), necessitating division by 4 [S5, unofficial].
+Calculates the projected area of a tetrahedron in normalized screen space to determine refinement criteria or culling. Uses cross products to compute wedge areas, which are twice the triangle area, then divides by four [S5, unofficial]. Project tetrahedron vertices $T, L, R, B$ to screen space using camera projection: $T \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(T)$, $L \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(L)$, $R \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(R)$, $B \leftarrow \text{camera.projectPoint}(B)$. Calculate area sum using cross products of vertex vectors: $\text{area} \leftarrow |(L-T)\times(R-T)|+|(R-T)\times(B-T)|$. Add remaining terms: $\text{area} \leftarrow \text{area}+|(B-T)\times(L-T)|+|(L-B)\times(R-B)|$. Return final area divided by 4: $\text{return area} / 4$. Triangles cover the total area twice in projection, and cross products yield wedge areas (twice triangle area), necessitating division by 4 [S5, unofficial].
 
 ### Pre-integrated classification for cell projection
-#### definition
-A method to determine color and opacity contribution by applying pre-integrated classification, using scalar values on front and back faces and thickness as texture coordinates for a 3D texture map storing volume ray integral values [S6].
-#### parameter
-$s_f$: Scalar value on the front face. $s_b$: Scalar value on the back face. $l$: Thickness resulting from scan converting the tetrahedron [S6].
